msgctxt "#30141"
msgid "'OFF' renders synchronously on the emulator thread: no worker pool, no command buffering, no thread synchronization. Numeric values use the threaded renderer with that many worker threads ('1' keeps the threaded pipeline with a single worker). 'All threads' uses the host's physical cores, at most 8. Every worker replays the whole command stream, so past 8 the duplicated work outweighs what more workers take off the spans, and a second thread on the same core only adds contention."
msgstr ""

